 "text": "Elisha Otis rose on a platform, then had its cable cut. It held, hoists of his day had a flaw. If the rope broke, the load fell. His break, rope tension held two catches back. If it snapped, a spring threw them into two thrails. He didn't invent the elevator. In 1854, he proved its safety break in public. Lesson, a new invention may need a test people can see before anyone wants it. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
